nce":[0,0,0,0.0,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":0}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":0.0259,"r5":0.0429,"r1_spy":0.0436,"r5_spy":0.0902,"r1_sector":0.0335,"r5_sector":0.0331,"etf":"XLF"}}],"quotes":[{"c":"EG 2018 Q3","e":"eg","d":"2018-10-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John Doucette","x":"As I have said before, this new paradigm of capital restructuring in SureTec and technology innovation, and other disruptive forces impacting our industry.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2019 Q1","e":"eg","d":"2019-05-08","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Elyse Greenspan","x":"But given what we’ve seen in the industry with Irma and the development with Irma, I mean can you give us a sense what kind of price increases would you need to see for this to be a successful renewal versus prices?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2019 Q1","e":"eg","d":"2019-05-08","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Elyse Greenspan","x":"If we get closer to 6/1 and prices fall short of expectations, is there a certain bar where Everest is going to walk away if they’re not able to recoup price increases after 2 successive years of losses?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2020 Q1","e":"eg","d":"2020-05-09","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Juan Andrade","x":"Retroactively restructuring the underpinnings of the workers' compensation system to shift the burden of proof of cost to employers and their insurers really undermines the spirit of the workers' compensation system.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2020 Q2","e":"eg","d":"2020-08-09","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Joshua Shanker","x":"If I may cede and I have a pool of risk that I'm raising prices on and I think improving margins on.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2021 Q4","e":"eg","d":"2022-02-10","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Juan Andrade","x":"An important part of this our continued investment in advanced tools, such as robotic process automation, artificial intelligence, and natural language processing, which creates greater operational efficiencies, and delivers better insights, enabling fact based decisions and best-in-class…","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2021 Q4","e":"eg","d":"2022-02-10","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Juan Andrade","x":"These talents, positions and promotions were part of a successful effort to optimize and streamline our structure, which is already benefiting the organization.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2022 Q3","e":"eg","d":"2022-10-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"James Williamson","x":"And in many cases they're absolutely willing to discuss ceding commission reduction on core casualty programs, in some cases related to an increase in available cat capacity or a restructuring of another program.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2023 Q1","e":"eg","d":"2023-05-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Juan Andrade","x":"We are streamlining and scaling our operations to serve the market with greater efficiency, connectivity and agility as we grow.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2023 Q2","e":"eg","d":"2023-07-27","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Juan Andrade","x":"The heart of reinsurance market contributed to positive pricing in the primary market.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2023 Q2","e":"eg","d":"2023-07-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Juan Andrade","x":"For example, the Australian market underwent a complete restructuring, moving away from frequency covers to true catastrophe structures.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2023 Q2","e":"eg","d":"2023-07-27","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Juan Andrade","x":"The enhancements we have made to augment our technology and streamline our infrastructure are yielding greater efficiencies and connectivity across our platform.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2023 Q4","e":"eg","d":"2024-02-08","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jim Williamson","x":"We did see some cap on formation up in the towers that caps price increases.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2024 Q3","e":"eg","d":"2024-10-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Josh Shanker","x":"Or are there firm orders that are telling you positive pricing is in the offering?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2025 Q1","e":"eg","d":"2025-05-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jim Williamson","x":"Everest has completed a thorough assessment of our exposure to the new tariff regime, and we believe prolonged tariffs at current levels would put modest upward pressure on loss cost trend.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2025 Q1","e":"eg","d":"2025-05-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Mark Kociancic","x":"As economic uncertainty has increased globally, our high-quality conservative portfolio remains well-positioned for the current environment with a relatively small exposure to investments that are meaningfully impacted by tariffs.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"EG 2025 Q2","e":"eg","d":"2025-07-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jim Williamson","x":"In terms of tariff activity and their impact on the business, I mean, obviously we monitor it, but at the end of the day, if you look at where we are international, we are barely beginning to scratch the surface of the markets we're competing in.","url":"https://s203.q4cdn.com/937887252/files/doc_financials/2025/q2/Everest-Group-Q2-2025-Earnings-Call-Transcript.pdf"},{"c":"EG 2025 Q2","e":"eg","d":"2025-07-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jim Williamson","x":"And then obviously the piece, when it comes to tariffs, the piece we do watch closely is loss cost trend here in the US.","url":"https://s203.q4cdn.com/937887252/files/doc_financials/2025/q2/Everest-Group-Q2-2025-Earnings-Call-Transcript.pdf"},{"c":"EG 2025 Q4","e":"eg","d":"2026-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark Kociancic","x":"As I previously noted, we expect there will be approximately $150 million of restructuring charges throughout 2026, associated with our exit from the commercial retail insurance business.","url":"https://s203.q4cdn.com/937887252/files/doc_financials/2025/q4/CORRECTED-TRANSCRIPT_-Everest-Group-Ltd-EG-US-Q4-2025-Earnings-Call-5-February-2026-8_00-AM-ET.pdf"},{"c":"EG 2025 Q4","e":"eg","d":"2026-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark Kociancic","x":"The underwriting-related expense ratio was 21.5%, with the increase driven by reduced casualty earned premium growth as well as onetime restructuring impacts that contributed 1.2 points to the increase, relating primarily to accelerated IT project depreciation.","url":"https://s203.q4cdn.com/937887252/files/doc_financials/2025/q4/CORRECTED-TRANSCRIPT_-Everest-Group-Ltd-EG-US-Q4-2025-Earnings-Call-5-February-2026-8_00-AM-ET.pdf"},{"c":"EG 2026 Q1","e":"eg","d":"2026-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Mark Kociancic","x":"As I previously noted, we expect there will be approximately $150 million of restructuring charges throughout 2026 associated with our exit from the commercial retail insurance business and we still expect some elevated real estate related costs in the fourth quarter, which we expect to mitigate…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/30/everest-group-eg-q1